Reconciliation (DR): Fable's 4/e_n^anti is the ONE-BIT COMPONENT: no one-bit
no-recovery policy beats the candidate on M for rho >= 4/e_anti. Kimi's full
law adds the zero-message L-witness: for rho<12, L_b = 1+rho/4 < 4 = L(candidate),
so SOMETHING in the hull stays alive below 12 regardless of n; for n>=8 the
one-bit branch 4/e_anti < 12 (since e_anti > 1/3) and the binding constraint
is the zero-message line at 12. For 3<=n<=7, 4/e_anti >= 12 and the one-bit
(antipodal) killer is binding. Consistent: rho_kill(n) = max(12, 4/e_anti(n)).
